lesson coding-one-card-is-wrong v=1 format=teach grade=1 unit=4 subject=coding levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "One card is wrong"
  goal "Find the card in a program that sends the robot the wrong way."

  look {
    scene 23x11 {
      row both at=canvas(1, 0) space=1 align=start {
        blocks b code=["right 2", "up 2", "right 2"] numbers=true words=false wrong=2
        maze m map=["S . . # .", ". # . # .", ". # . . F", ". . . # ."] code=["right 2", "up 2", "right 2"]
      }
    }
    say """
      The robot bumped into the edge, so something in the program is wrong. Run it one card at a
      time and watch where it first goes the wrong way. That card is the bug: it says up when the
      path goes down.
      """
  }
  do {
    practice coding.bump-card count=2 seed=3
    show coding.which-card k=2 easy-k=0
    show coding.which-card k=0 easy-k=3 hard-k=1
    practice coding.turtle-wrong-card count=2 seed=5
    show coding.fix-number a=2 b=1 w=1 d=1 hard-a=4 hard-b=2 hard-w=2
    show coding.fix-number a=3 b=2 w=2 d=-1 easy-a=3 easy-b=1 easy-w=1 hard-w=1
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show coding.bug-hidden w=3 e=1 easy-w=1 hard-w=4 hard-e=-1
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show coding.shorter-program k=0
  }
  remember {
    say "Find where the robot first goes wrong. The card that did it is the bug."
  }

  grown-ups """
    A bug is information, not a failure: where the robot went wrong says which card to look at.
    Resist pointing at the card. Ask where the robot first stopped going the right way. The
    turtle's pale shape and the burst where the robot hits a rock are two more ways a bug shows
    itself. In the two-star question there is no trail to follow, so the program has to be walked
    with a finger. The three-star question is about making a working program shorter, which is a
    different thing from making it right.
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the wrong card points the wrong way, so the line the robot drew shows it at once, and the bump comes on the first block."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the wrong card has a number one out and sits late in the program, so the whole path has to be walked to find it."
  }
}
